<comment datatype='string'>&lt;a href=&quot;/compound?orgid=META&amp;id=TIRON&quot;&gt;tiron&lt;/a&gt; ((sodium-4,5-dihydroxy-1,3-benzene disulfonate), also known as tiferron, is a a hydrophilic chelating agent that has been tried in treatment of a number of experimental metal toxicities including manganese [&lt;a href=&quot;http://www.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/pubmed/7594197&quot;&gt;Sanchez95&lt;/a&gt;], uranium [&lt;a href=&quot;http://www.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/pubmed/8497868&quot;&gt;Bosque93&lt;/a&gt;], lead [&lt;a href=&quot;http://www.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/pubmed/3794712&quot;&gt;Pocock87&lt;/a&gt;], vanadium [&lt;a href=&quot;http://www.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/pubmed/7795320&quot;&gt;Domingo95&lt;/a&gt;] and beryllium [&lt;a href=&quot;http://www.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/pubmed/12185411&quot;&gt;Sharma02&lt;/a&gt;, &lt;a href=&quot;http://www.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/pubmed/15260107&quot;&gt;Mathur04&lt;/a&gt;]. It also is a &lt;a href=&quot;/META/NEW-IMAGE?type=REACTION&amp;object=SUPEROX-DISMUT-RXN&quot;&gt;superoxide dismutase&lt;/a&gt; mimetic and a cell membrane permeable scavenger of &lt;a href=&quot;/compound?orgid=META&amp;id=SUPER-OXIDE&quot;&gt;superoxide&lt;/a&gt; anion [&lt;a href=&quot;http://www.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/pubmed/11387504&quot;&gt;Bryan01&lt;/a&gt;].</comment>
